Practice save scroll reading! Use the JMP's reading rules :-)
(Spoilers?)

1) AVOID READING UNKNOWN ORIGIN SCROLLS! Identify first.

If you really can't - then

2) Check the blessed/cused status of your scrolls first - avoid at all costs
   reading the cursed ones before identifying.
3) Read scrolls shortly after you entered a new level (still in the first
   room) - minimize loss if amnesia, maximize gain if magic mapping/detection
4) Take off all valuable armor first (but keep something worthless, like
   an orcish helm, on) - esp. if you haven't seen destroy armor yet.
5) If you haven't seen scroll of fire yet - drop all other potions scrolls
   and books first.
6) If you haven't seen identify yet - be sure that you have something worth
   identyfying (rings, amulets, other scrolls if you didn't have to drop them
   in 5).

Now, you can try to read. The worst thing that can happen is probably a loss
of a few HP to fire or a loss of a few spells to amnesia (therefore read 
scrolls before the books).
 
Ah, somebody could ask how to identify scrolls before reading at least one...

